WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.210
A whole AI

00:00:01.022 --> 00:00:02.048
chat OS in

00:00:01.859 --> 00:00:03.227
24 kilobytes

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.811
A developer wrote

00:00:04.623 --> 00:00:06.261
a bootable x86

00:00:06.097 --> 00:00:07.382
operating system in

00:00:07.193 --> 00:00:08.584
pure assembly that

00:00:08.396 --> 00:00:09.575
runs the Qwen3

00:00:09.387 --> 00:00:10.271
0 .

00:00:10.083 --> 00:00:11.108
6B model

00:00:11.285 --> 00:00:12.417
with no Linux

00:00:12.359 --> 00:00:13.408
no C and

00:00:13.219 --> 00:00:14.009
no libc

00:00:14.542 --> 00:00:15.615
It cold boots

00:00:15.426 --> 00:00:16.487
to an interactive

00:00:16.299 --> 00:00:17.666
multi-turn chat in

00:00:17.478 --> 00:00:19.129
74 to 94

00:00:18.941 --> 00:00:19.848
milliseconds

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:20.827
with the model

00:00:20.639 --> 00:00:21.747
mapped straight from

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:22.725
RAM on huge

00:00:22.537 --> 00:00:23.315
pages

00:00:23.846 --> 00:00:25.060
Under KVM on

00:00:24.872 --> 00:00:25.945
a sixteen core

00:00:25.756 --> 00:00:27.136
EPYC it decodes

00:00:26.947 --> 00:00:29.022
about 135 tokens

00:00:28.834 --> 00:00:29.612
per second

00:00:29.778 --> 00:00:30.650
and it even

00:00:30.462 --> 00:00:31.452
runs live on

00:00:31.263 --> 00:00:32.643
a diskless Proxmox

00:00:32.454 --> 00:00:33.539
virtual machine

00:00:34.062 --> 00:00:35.076
Full story on

00:00:34.887 --> 00:00:35.783
the dashboard
